// green/red instead of the map's colour, so a road-vs-ground meter can be computed against the
// shader's actual lane rather than against coordinates picked off a screenshot (which is how a
// round-13 road delta got measured against the crater interior instead of against the sand).
// Read only under SHOT, like every other bisect switch in this file.
const MASK_DBG = !!SHOT && P.has('maskdbg');
// ...and its sibling: the terrain's world NORMAL, so finding 3's assertion ("two cliff patches
// whose world normals differ by >60 deg in the sun plane must differ by dL* >= 12") can be run
// as a real test over every rock fragment in a frame instead of over two hand-picked squares.
const NORM_DBG = !!SHOT && P.has('normdbg');
// r13 WORLD 2/5/11 — shadow-guard bisect. `&shddbg=1` writes the guard's TARGET colour into the
// shadow, `&shddbg=2` writes its gate. SHOT-only, like every other switch here.
const SHD_DBG = (SHOT && P.has('shddbg')) ? (parseInt(P.get('shddbg')) || 1) : 0;
const U_TILEN = { value: P.has('notile') ? 0.0 : tier === 'mobile' ? 0.5 : 1.0 };
// §B item 4 — ROAD ALBEDO AUTHORITY, and WHICH maps need it. Round 10 measured road-vs-adjacent
// -ground ΔL* at 1.1-2.3 on maps 3 and 5 against a target of 8. Those are exactly the two maps
// whose ground is pale sand/ash: on grass, snow or heather the road's own brown carries the
// contrast for free, and on a bleached basin it has no value authority at all. Keyed on the
// ground TILE rather than on a map id, so the rule states its own reason.
// r11 WORLD 5 §7. 0.700 was itself the cap that held the delta under target: a road at 70% of
// the adjacent soil's LUMINANCE is delta-L* 6.4 against an acceptance of 8, so the guarantee was
// guaranteeing the wrong number. 0.58 lands delta-L* 9.4 with the same construction. Extended to
// the moor as a looser guarantee (0.72), because r11 §7 asks for the meter on EVERY map and the
// Barrowmoor is a dusk map where a hard clamp would punch the lane into the frame's black tail.
// r11 WORLD 9 — near-period multiplier for the GROUND tile only (see the note at the tap). The
// vegetated tiles carry blade/twig structure that has to land under a metre to read as turf; sand
// and snow carry dune structure that must NOT be halved, or a drift becomes corduroy.
// ══ r14 WORLD 12 (a) — "DROP THE NEAR TILING BAND FROM ~1.5 wu TO ~0.5 wu" ══════════════════
// Measured 3x3 Laplacian energy: _charger sand 4.6 against _wardhit road 20.1 and closeup
// meadow 11.5 — the sand is three times flatter than anything else in the build, and 1.5 wu is
// why: at the closeup camera a detail texel on sand covers 4-6 screen px, so the tile is
// MAGNIFIED and every feature in it is a soft smear by the time it is lit. TILE_SN is 1/1.5 wu,
// so this multiplier is the per-kind near period. Grass and heather go to 0.5 wu (3x), which is
// what puts a blade under two screen px at the gameplay-close camera; sand and snow go to
